> This design has several advantages:
> 
> - The columns directly express the mitigation-relevant comparison: **lower warming versus higher warming**.
> - When you fill the currently missing cells, the table naturally becomes more persuasive and useful without redesign.
> - Splitting 2050 and 2100 prevents an eight-column sprawl.
> - The reader does not have to infer that “2050, 1.7–2.1°C” and “2100, 2.4–3.0°C” represent distinct warming conditions.
> 
